// viewFlattenLimit bounds how deep an overlay chain a published view grows
// before the next commit collapses the chain's overlays into one. Without a
// bound the chain would gain one map per commit for the life of the store and
// memory would track cumulative commits. Collapsing merges only the overlays
// above the flat base — exactly the keys touched since that base was built —
// so the temporary allocation a commit group makes stays proportional to the
// keys its own commits touched and never grows with the live keyspace, no
// matter how many commits queue up. The merged overlay is freshly allocated
// and the base is shared, so views already published stay immutable.
const viewFlattenLimit = 64

